{:edb/db-before-t 2700 :edb/db-after-t 2701 :edb/tx-data [[13194139536013 50 #inst "2026-10-15T18:42:56.997Z" 13194139536013 17592186045443 true] [17592186129262 1038 #edb/ref 17592186557447 13194139536013 17592186045443 true] [17592186129262 1038 #edb/ref 17592186557450 13194139536013 17592186045443 true] [17592186129262 1038 #edb/ref 17592186557452 13194139536013 17592186045443 true] [17592186129262 1038 #edb/ref 17592186557458 13194139536013 17592186045443 true] [17592186129262 1038 #edb/ref 17592186557460 13194139536013 17592186045443 true] [17592186129262 1038 #edb/ref 17592186557470 13194139536013 17592186045443 true] [17592186129262 1038 #edb/ref 17592186557473 13194139536013 17592186045443 true] [17592186129262 1038 #edb/ref 17592186557489 13194139536013 17592186045443 true] [17592186129262 1040 #edb/ref 17592186557502 13194139536013 17592186045443 true] [17592186557446 1080 "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{4}{3}" 13194139536013 17592186045443 true] [17592186557446 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139536013 17592186045443 true] [17592186557446 1083 #uuid "0bde0c95-87d9-5021-b422-7d119cac0a2f" 13194139536013 17592186045443 true] [17592186557447 1068 #edb/ref 17592186557479 13194139536013 17592186045443 true] [17592186557447 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139536013 17592186045443 true] [17592186557447 1071 "Use a change of variables to calculate the area of the finite region $D$ in the first quadrant bounded by the following curves and lines.\n$y = \\frac{3}{x}, y = \\frac{7}{x}, y = 4x, y = 5x$" 13194139536013 17592186045443 true] [17592186557447 1072 #uuid "122c57cf-cfe9-5e24-b30b-49b9810a796b" 13194139536013 17592186045443 true] [17592186557447 1074 "The area of the required region is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}dxdy.\n$$\n\nLet's define a transformation $T$ as follows: \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWe'll assume this transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane to our region $D$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\nTo compute the required area, we will use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}dxdy={∬}_{Δ}|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\text{ }dudv,\n$$\n\n  \n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$\n\nTo compute the required area, we proceed in five steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Find a suitable change of variables.\n\nNotice that we can rewrite the equations of our curves as follows:\n\n$$\nxy=3,\\,xy=7,\\,\\frac{y}{x}=4,\\,\\frac{y}{x}=5\n$$\n\nThis suggests the following change of variables:\n\n$$\nu=xy,\\,v=\\frac{y}{x}\n$$\n\nThis change of variables gives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) \\\\ v(x,y)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $D$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$ \n\nWe substitute $u=xy$ into the equations of the first and second curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & xy=3\\,⟹\\,u=3 \\\\  & xy=7\\,⟹\\,u=7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAnd we substitute $v=\\frac{y}{x}$ into the equations of the third and fourth curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\frac{y}{x}=4\\,⟹\\,v=4 \\\\  & \\frac{y}{x}=5\\,⟹\\,v=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our domain in the $uv$-plane is the following rectangle:\n\n$$\nΔ=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,3\\le u\\le 7,\\,4\\le v\\le 5\\}\n$$\n\n![](images/3d/3dc524083463c8c370ff1f79d68093f0d3f2c2fe1ceb5cd47824782e35a0bac9.png)\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & \\frac{∂u}{∂y} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & \\frac{∂v}{∂y}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}y & x \\\\ -\\frac{y}{x^2} & \\frac{1}{x}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{y}{x}+\\frac{y}{x} \\\\  & =2v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 4**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}={(\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)})}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{2v}.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$  In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 5**: Compute the required area.\n\nWe calculate the required area by performing the change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\text{d}x\\text{d}y & ={∬}_{Δ}|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={∬}_{Δ}\\frac{1}{2v}\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{3}^{7}\\,\\text{d}u{\\int }_{4}^{5}\\frac{1}{v}\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (7-3)\\cdot (\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{5}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536013 17592186045443 true] [17592186557448 1080 "\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{5}{3}" 13194139536013 17592186045443 true] [17592186557448 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139536013 17592186045443 true] [17592186557448 1083 #uuid "12fb765d-ae64-5832-b007-b74f3340d57d" 13194139536013 17592186045443 true] [17592186557449 1075 #edb/ref 17592186557457 13194139536013 17592186045443 true] [17592186557449 1075 #edb/ref 17592186557467 13194139536013 17592186045443 true] [17592186557449 1075 #edb/ref 17592186557480 13194139536013 17592186045443 true] [17592186557449 1075 #edb/ref 17592186557490 13194139536013 17592186045443 true] [17592186557449 1075 #edb/ref 17592186557495 13194139536013 17592186045443 true] [17592186557449 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139536013 17592186045443 true] [17592186557449 1077 "selection" 13194139536013 17592186045443 true] [17592186557449 1078 #edb/ref 17592186557495 13194139536013 17592186045443 true] [17592186557449 1079 #uuid "18f802c8-f27c-572f-a462-5834e5ade5cc" 13194139536013 17592186045443 true] [17592186557450 1068 #edb/ref 17592186557471 13194139536013 17592186045443 true] [17592186557450 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139536013 17592186045443 true] [17592186557450 1071 "Use a change of variables to calculate the area of the 